# Path, bucket, purpose. An inventory of what the Sublet port of FFmpeg's own pools cost beside the
# allocator, for I1. Paths are relative to capstone/ports/ffmpeg/. The allocator changes themselves
# are the two patches, counted by capstone/tests/port-effort.py against their sibling .classes
# files, not here.
sublet/ffmpeg-9.0.1-0001-avbufferpool-on-sublet.patch allocator AVBufferPool: blocks from the heap, entries carved, a take per get, a give per return, one revoke per block at the end
sublet/ffmpeg-9.0.1-0002-refstruct-on-sublet.patch allocator refstruct: the header beside the object, found by address after a probe; AVRefStructPool entries carved as in 0001
sublet/ffsublet.h glue the interface the patched pools call, copied into libavutil by prepare-source.sh --sublet
app/src/capstone-domain/ffsublet.c allocator the level below: linear blocks from the Sublet heap, carve, take, give, the heap's free of each block, and the counts
../musl-capstone/runtime/sublet_heap.c allocator __capstone_sublet_malloc_linear and __capstone_sublet_free_linear, the heap's linear lend and its revoke (added for this port)
app/host/prepare-source.sh glue --sublet: the app's patches plus these, keyed by every file applied
app/host/build-domain.sh glue FFAPP_POOL=sublet builds the port; FFAPP_POOL=stock is its one-macro control
app/host/run-qemu.sh glue the port's arm takes no payload region: its pools live on the heap
app/host/run-safety.sh test the poolsublet and poolstock arms
app/host/safety-expect.txt test the pre-registered verdicts of fixtures 11-17 on both arms
app/src/capstone-domain/ffapp_domain.c test prints the pools' counts after each stage
